    "what_it_is": "Beta-copaene is a bridged sesquiterpene, a type of volatile aromatic molecule produced by plants to interact with their environment. As a volatile organic compound found in flowers and fruits, it contributes to the complex scents and flavors of the natural world. You likely encounter it when peeling a fresh citrus fruit or brushing past fragrant garden herbs.",
